
# HTML Tables - Complete Guide

## Introduction

HTML tables are used to display data in **rows and columns**.
They are useful for presenting structured information such as **student records, product lists, schedules, pricing tables, and reports**.

A table in HTML is created using the `<table>` tag along with rows (`<tr>`) and cells (`<th>` and `<td>`).

---

# Basic Table Structure

```html
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Heading 1</th>
    <th>Heading 2</th>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td>Data 1</td>
    <td>Data 2</td>
  </tr>
</table>
```

---

# Important HTML Table Tags

| Tag       | Meaning      | Purpose               |
| --------- | ------------ | --------------------- |
| `<table>` | Table        | Creates the table     |
| `<tr>`    | Table Row    | Creates a row         |
| `<th>`    | Table Header | Creates a header cell |
| `<td>`    | Table Data   | Creates a data cell   |

---

# Simple Table Example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Table Example</title>
</head>

<body>

<table border="1">
  <tr>
    <th>Name</th>
    <th>Age</th>
    <th>City</th>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td>Navya</td>
    <td>24</td>
    <td>Rajahmundry</td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td>Rahul</td>
    <td>23</td>
    <td>Hyderabad</td>
  </tr>

</table>

</body>
</html>
```

---

# Table Attributes

## Border

Adds a border around the table.

```html
<table border="1">
```

---

## Cell Padding

Adds space inside table cells.

```html
<table border="1" cellpadding="10">
```

---

## Cell Spacing

Adds space between table cells.

```html
<table border="1" cellspacing="5">
```

---

# Colspan (Merge Columns)

The `colspan` attribute merges multiple columns into a single column.

```html
<table border="1">
<tr>
<th colspan="2">Student Info</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Name</td>
<td>Navya</td>
</tr>
</table>
```

---

# Rowspan (Merge Rows)

The `rowspan` attribute merges multiple rows.

```html
<table border="1">
<tr>
<th rowspan="2">Name</th>
<td>Navya</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Rahul</td>
</tr>
</table>
```

---

# Table Sections

HTML tables can be divided into three sections.

| Tag       | Purpose      |
| --------- | ------------ |
| `<thead>` | Table header |
| `<tbody>` | Table body   |
| `<tfoot>` | Table footer |

Example:

```html
<table border="1">

<thead>
<tr>
<th>Name</th>
<th>Marks</th>
</tr>
</thead>

<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Navya</td>
<td>90</td>
</tr>
</tbody>

<tfoot>
<tr>
<td>Total</td>
<td>90</td>
</tr>
</tfoot>

</table>
```

---

# Styling Tables with CSS

```html
<style>
table {
  border-collapse: collapse;
  width: 50%;
}

th, td {
  border: 1px solid black;
  padding: 10px;
  text-align: center;
}

th {
  background-color: lightgray;
}
</style>
```

---

# Example: Product Table

```html
<table>
<tr>
<th>Product</th>
<th>Price</th>
<th>Quantity</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Cake</td>
<td>₹500</td>
<td>2</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Donut</td>
<td>₹100</td>
<td>5</td>
</tr>
</table>
```

---

# Real World Uses of Tables

HTML tables are commonly used for:

* Student records
* Product listings
* Timetables
* Pricing tables
* Scoreboards
* Financial reports

---

# Important Note

Tables should be used **only for displaying tabular data**.

Do **NOT** use tables for webpage layout.
Modern layouts are created using **CSS Flexbox or CSS Grid**.

---

# Conclusion

HTML tables are an essential concept for displaying structured data on webpages.
Understanding table tags, attributes, and styling helps create clean and organized data presentation.
